  "caseFindings": {
    "HR-A03": "Negative-control-like miss: all three bets prefer a more general/metaproductive pilot and defer the specialized line, while the hidden local outcome rewards specialization under concentrated repeated demand. Generality is not automatically frontier value.",
    "HR-A05": "3/3 choose the animal-free conductor/electrolyte intervention and preserve unresolved bioelectricity; close historical match.",
    "HR-A08": "3/3 reject one-shot acceptance and require reproduction/realistic testing; 2/3 explicitly continue both solution families while the third defers but does not abandon astronomy.",
    "HR-A09": "3/3 combine model-guided mapping with independent distributed regional checks; close match to the Smith/Greenough historical correction."
  },
  "validityBoundary": "A frontier model may already know these historical structures from pretraining even after de-identification. The replay therefore tests whether a bounded packet elicits useful research-control behavior, not whether the model independently rediscovered history. Identity guessing was prohibited but structural-memory leakage cannot be ruled out."
